### README.md  [docs]
- Browser-based screen sharing with vision analysis. Works with any multimodal LLM from any PC on your network.
- ## What It Does
- - **WebRTC Screen Sharing** - Share screen from any browser
- - **Visual Analysis** - Analyze screens with AI vision
- - **Model Agnostic** - Works with Gemini, Claude, Qwen3-VL, etc.
- - **Remote Access** - Auto-detects correct URL for network sharing
- ### Prerequisites
- 1. **Clawdbot** v2026.1.17+ with multimodal LLM configured
- 2. **Node.js** (for backend server)
- 3. **Modern Browser** (Chrome, Edge, Firefox)
- 4. **Optional**: ImageMagick (Linux fallback)
- ### Quick Start
- # 1. Install skill
- # Or manual:
- git clone https://github.com/masoudy-engineering/clawdbot-skills.git
- # 2. Install dependencies (Linux only)
- sudo apt-get install imagemagick
- # 3. Start backend server
- cd ~/.clawdbot/skills/screen-monitor/references
- node backend-endpoint.js
- # Server runs on port 18795
- ```
