- ### Configure Multimodal LLM
- Screen-Monitor requires a vision-capable model:
- clawdbot configure
- # Select one of:
- # - Google Gemini 2.0 Flash
- # - Claude 3.5 Sonnet
- # - Qwen3-VL (local)
- ### 1. Get Screen Share Link
- User: "Give me the screen share link"
- Agent: "Open http://10.0.0.10:18795/screen-share"
- ### 2. Share Your Screen
- 1. Click the link (from any PC on network)
- 2. Click "Start Sharing"
- 3. Select window/screen to share
- 4. Browser captures frames every 3 seconds
- ### 3. Ask Questions
- User: "What's wrong with this error message?"
- Agent: [Analyzes current screen frame]
-        "I see a Python NameError on line 42..."
- ## Two Modes
- ### Mode A: Fast Share (WebRTC)
- - Best for quick visual checks
- - Works from any PC
- - No installation on client
- - 3-second frame updates
- ### Mode B: Browser Control (Chrome Extension)
- - Best for automation
- - Can click/type in browser
- - Requires Chrome extension
- - Full browser control
- ## Troubleshooting
- **Link doesn't work from other PC?**
- - Check firewall allows port 18795
- - Ensure backend server is running
- - Try: `curl http://localhost:18795/screen-share`
- **"No active screen share"?**
- - Click "Start Sharing" in browser
- - Check browser console for errors
- - Grant screen sharing permission
- **Vision analysis fails?**
- ⚠️  Your model doesn't support images
-    Switch to multimodal LLM: clawdbot configure
- ## Technical Details
- - **Port**: 18795 (customizable)
- - **Frame Storage**: `/tmp/clawdbot-screen-latest.png`
- - **Capture Interval**: 3 seconds
- - **Format**: PNG, base64 encoded
- - **Model**: Uses Clawdbot's configured model
- ## Network Access
- **LAN**: Auto-detects your IP
- **Tailscale**: Works with VPN
- **Localhost**: Fallback mode
- ## Contributing
- Report issues: https://github.com/masoudy-engineering/clawdbot-skills/issues
